> **The capstone's purpose is the method, not the score.** A learner who repairs four faults with clean evidence, honest logs, and a good reflection has passed. A learner who reaches green by widening a guardrail has not.

### Grading against the bars

| Bar | Requirement |
|---|---|
| **Minimum** | seven faults named with an evidence-backed area; ≥ 5 with a verified repair in the change log; seven reflection blocks completed |
| **Full** | minimum, plus `capstone-check.sh` exits `0`, the inventory is exactly eight and green, it holds on a second reading, every change went through one of the four paths, and no guardrail is wider than its design |

**Check this last point explicitly in the debrief:**

```bash
kubectl --context k3d-workload auth can-i create clusterroles.rbac.authorization.k8s.io \
  --as=system:serviceaccount:argocd-access:argocd-manager       # must still be: no
argocd proj get team-a                                          # unchanged from Lab 5
kubectl --context k3d-mgmt -n argocd get cm argocd-rbac-cm -o yaml | grep -A5 policy.csv
```

